{"orgCode":"0956","name":"California Debt and Investment Advisory Commission","agencyCode":"0010","agencyName":"Legislative, Judicial, and Executive","description":"The mission of the California Debt and Investment Advisory Commission is to support and improve the practice of public finance in California by providing responsive and reliable information, analysis, and training. The Commission assists California state and local governments to monitor, issue, and manage public debt and to safely and prudently invest public funds.\n\nThe Commission consists of nine members including the State Treasurer, who serves as chairperson; the Governor or, upon his designation, the Director of Finance; the State Controller; two local government finance officers appointed by the State Treasurer; two members of the Assembly appointed by the Speaker of the Assembly; and two members of the Senate appointed by the Senate Committee on Rules.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":3186,"cy":4341,"by":4345},"positions":{"py":17.9,"cy":21,"by":21},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":57,"cy":180,"by":180}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/0010/0956","kind":"department","name":"California Debt and Investment Advisory Commission","code":"0956","amounts":{"py":3186,"cy":4341,"by":4345},"positions":{"py":17.9,"cy":21,"by":21},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":3186,"cy":4341,"by":4345}},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0956/0800","kind":"program","name":"California Debt and Investment Advisory Commission","code":"0800","amounts":{"py":3186,"cy":4341,"by":4345},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":3186,"cy":4341,"by":4345}},"positions":{"py":17.9,"cy":21,"by":21},"description":"0800 - CALIFORNIA DEBT AND INVESTMENT ADVISORY COMMISSION\n\nThe Commission's primary objective is to enhance the knowledge of public officials with respect to the administration and issuance of public debt and the investment of public funds. The Commission achieves this objective by performing functions in three principal areas, including:\n\n• Data Collection and Analysis - Serves as a clearinghouse of debt issued by California public entities and nonprofit student loan corporations.\n\n• Continuing Education - Provides educational seminars, workshops, and conferences to public officials on municipal debt and public fund investment topics. In addition, the Commission provides technical assistance to public officials and taxpayers through direct interaction and public forums to disseminate relevant information.\n\n• Policy Research - Undertakes original research on the issuance and administration of public debt and on the investment of public funds. Research results are published in the form of reports, issue briefs, or articles and are disseminated in printed and electronic forms.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3243,"cy":4521,"by":4525}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0956/0800/f0171","kind":"fund","name":"California Debt and Investment Advisory Commission Fund","code":"0171","amounts":{"py":3186,"cy":4341,"by":4345},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":3186,"cy":4341,"by":4345}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3186,"cy":4341,"by":4345}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0956/0800/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":57,"cy":180,"by":180},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":57,"cy":180,"by":180}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":57,"cy":180,"by":180}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":57,"cy":180,"by":180}}}],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/0956","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/0956"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/0010/0956.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"DEPARTMENT AUTHORITY\n\nGovernment Code Sections 8855-8859."},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":57,"cy":180,"by":180}}},"funding":{"id":"exp/0010/0956/f